<item>
<title>Members only!</title>
<link>https://www.theapplepi.org/members-only/</link>
<pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
<dc:creator><![CDATA[pi-editor]]></dc:creator>
<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.theapplepi.org/members-only.html</guid>
<description></description>
<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Members-Only Presentation Materials</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Using the link below requires access to the Pi site on groups.io -- and therefore a Pi membership.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><li>If you are currently logged into groups.io, the link will take you to the Presentations section of the site. Here you will have access to various presentation materials and non-public videos of select General Meetings and tech demos.</li><li>​If you are not currently logged into groups.io, you will be prompted to enter your groups.io username and password before you can access the materials.</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:buttons {"layout":{"type":"flex","justifyContent":"center"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-buttons"><!-- wp:button -->
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://applepi.groups.io/g/main/files/Presentations">Members-only link to groups.io &gt; Files &gt; Presentations</a></div>
<!-- /wp:button --></div>
<!-- /wp:buttons -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":2} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Time Travel to our earlier website</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In 2024, the Pi launched this new website and it is our focus moving forward. However, the Pi&#x27;s prior site is still operational and contains a trove of historical and technical information. There are two Time Machine &quot;tickets&quot; below that will take you back in time. The first ticket will deposit you at the Home page for the venerable wap.org website (doing business at the same location since 1978). For our older longtime members who still use a wap.org email address and/or use the Pi’s old TCS Forum, find links to these at the top of the wap.org page.  Your journey using the second ticket will end at the door to the Pi Journals library that contains Pi Journals and newsletters from February 1979. For those interested in our backstory, this is the place to visit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:buttons {"layout":{"type":"flex","justifyContent":"center"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-buttons"><!-- wp:button -->
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://wap.org/">Ticket 1: Take me to wap.org</a></div>
<!-- /wp:button --></div>
<!-- /wp:buttons -->

<!-- wp:buttons {"layout":{"type":"flex","justifyContent":"center"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-buttons"><!-- wp:button -->
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://wap.org/journal/showcase/">Ticket 2: Take me to the Journal archives</a></div>
<!-- /wp:button --></div>
<!-- /wp:buttons -->]]></content:encoded>
<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[]]></excerpt:encoded>
