</item>
<item>
<title>Why Join groups.io</title>
<link>https://www.theapplepi.org/why-join-groupsio/</link>
<pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400</pubDate>
<dc:creator><![CDATA[pi-editor]]></dc:creator>
<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.theapplepi.org/why-join-groupsio.html</guid>
<description></description>
<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph {"align":"center"} -->
<p class="has-text-align-center"><span style="color:#5040ae;font-size:2.4rem">What is groups.io?</span></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pi members use groups.io to share information, help each other, and request assistance. groups.io is an online service that supports both interactive email and posting on the Pi&#x27;s groups.io website. Between meetings, groups.io is where all the Pi action happens, and it is your direct line for technical assistance.<br><br>Note that groups.io is distinct from Join It, the Pi&#x27;s membership management service. Establishing a separate groups.io account is required to get the most from your Pi membership. groups.io is the place you will communicate with other Pi members, post information, and provide assistance  <strong><a href="https://applepi.groups.io/register" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="color:#5040ae">Click here</span></a></strong> to establish your groups.io account. Creating your account will automatically subscribe you to the Pi mailing list.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"align":"center"} -->
<p class="has-text-align-center"><span style="color:#5040ae;font-size:2.4rem">Why join groups.io?</span></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><span style="font-size:1.35rem">Because it&#x27;s your place to engage and stay on top of what&#x27;s happening in the Pi.<br>In groups.io you can:</span>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><li><span style="font-size:1.35rem">Generally Stay in Touch</span><br>The main Apple Pi area of groups.io is the location where members keep up with what&#x27;s happening in the Pi. Reading the posts here will help you understand what&#x27;s new with technology (hardware and software) and make you the smartest person in the room (assuming you choose your rooms carefully!). Oh, and don&#x27;t worry, lurking is allowed. --meaning there is no pressure to actively post to the site or to interact with posts made by others. We love it if you play but we all spend some time on the bleachers.</li><li><span style="font-size:1.35rem">View the Pi Events Calendars</span><br>When is the next General Meeting or Clubhouse Saturday? What&#x27;s scheduled upcoming in my special interest group? Find out what else is going on. The events Calendars are only available in group.io and contain the Zoom links for virtual meetings.</li><li><span style="font-size:1.35rem">Post Your Questions</span><br>Something got you stumped? Need a bit of assistance with a new feature or two in the latest Mac or iOS release? Help may be available by posting your conundrum and requesting some thoughts. The answer may appear in a reply to your post or might present itself with an offer of some one-on-one assistance.</li><li><span style="font-size:1.35rem">Provide and Receive Answers</span><br>While it feels good to get your questions answered, and it feels even better to help someone else. Here&#x27;s where you can share what you know.</li><li><span style="font-size:1.35rem">Go Deep With SIGs</span><br>SIGs are Special Interest Groups providing an opportunity to dive deeper with those sharing your particular passion, such as Photography. SIGs have their own areas within groups.io and where members of each SIG can geek-out knowing they are &quot;talking&quot; to others with similar interests and without posting to a more general audience.</li><li><span style="font-size:1.35rem">Share</span><br> Share your experiences and expertise with the members (or just the latest tip or trick you&#x27;ve discovered). You will likely find members who will share your excitement over a new tech purchase or cheer you on as you increase your hardware or software mastery.</li><li><span style="font-size:1.35rem">Request One-on-One Assistance</span><br>Sometimes we just need a little additional assistance. There is no guarantee that one of our members will always be able to come up with a solution, but we are often willing to try. Perhaps a personal phone call or and individual Zoom session will do the trick.</li><li>[additional items?]</li></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->]]></content:encoded>
<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[]]></excerpt:encoded>
<wp:post_id>169</wp:post_id>
